</html></richcontent>
<node TEXT="Description" ID="ID_30953802" CREATED="1789668791663" MODIFIED="1789670063712"><richcontent TYPE="DETAILS">
<html>
  <head>
    
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>
      it receives the returned reply from run_checklist that prompted Gemma3:4b. This reply is called raw_output, and contains the same information (see raw_output). Using Regular Expressions (re) and strip(), parse_entries will break the raw_output into blocks, then split each block in a item, answer, and quote match driven the text inside the block. it'll take that item, answer, and quote matches and append them onto the entries variable in a loop until all of Gemma3:4b's reply is a proper dictionary list variable. The list variable, entries, is then returned.
    </p>
  </body>
</html></richcontent>
</node>
